overview.proofStrategy:
**Counting step**: For A ⊆ X with |A| = n:
- `{B ⊆ X : Disjoint B A} = powerset(X \setminus A)`, so |(·)| = 2^{|X|−n}
- `{B ⊆ X : A ⊆ B}` bijects with `powerset(X \setminus A)` via B ↦ X\setminus B, so |(·)| = 2^{|X|−n}
- Union: at most 2·2^{|X|−n} bad-due-to-A subsets

**Union bound**: |total bad| ≤ ∑_{A∈F} |bad-due-to-A| ≤ |F| · 2·2^{|X|−n}

**Conclusion**: |goodSets F| = 2^|X| − |bad| ≥ 2^|X| − |F|·2^{|X|−n+1}
